<title>USA: Minneapolis council to vote on stadium site - report.</title>
<headline>Minneapolis council to vote on stadium site - report.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Minneapolis City Council is scheduled to vote Friday on a site for a new Minnesota Twins baseball team stadium, the Minneapolis Star Tribune reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>Council members will be asked to choose from four sites, the newspaper reported, despite the fact that no financing plan is in place for the stadium.</p>
<p>According to the newspaper, Minnesota Gov. Arne Carlson has urged the city to pick a site for the stadium.</p>
<p>--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647</p>
